AI Overview        
To configure the ST7789P3 1.14" 135x240 LCD display on your M5Stick S3 using ESPHome, 
you can use either the modern mipi_spi platform (recommended) or the older ili9xxx platform.
Since the ST7789P3 requires custom offsets and color-inversion rules, the configuration below 
uses standard esp-idf and the optimized SPI settings for the M5Stack S3 pin layout.
ESPHome Configuration YAML

esphome:
  name: m5stick-s3
  friendly_name: M5Stick S3

esp32:
  board: esp32-s3-devkitc-1
  framework:
    type: esp-idf

# Configure the SPI bus matching the M5Stick S3 internal screen pins
spi:
  clk_pin: GPIO17
  mosi_pin: GPIO21

# Setup backlight control 
output:
  - platform: ledc
    pin: GPIO16
    id: backlight_pwm

light:
  - platform: monochromatic
    output: backlight_pwm
    name: "Display Backlight"
    id: display_backlight
    restore_mode: ALWAYS_ON

# Display Configuration
display:
  - platform: ili9xxx
    model: st7789v
    id: m5_display
    cs_pin: GPIO15
    dc_pin: GPIO33
    reset_pin: GPIO34
    
    # Physical screen boundaries & offsets for the 1.14" 135x240 panel
    dimensions:
      height: 240
      width: 135
      offset_height: 40
      offset_width: 52
      
    # Matching the screen layout orientation (Adjust swap/mirror to taste)
    transform:
      swap_xy: false
      mirror_x: false
      mirror_y: false
      
    invert_colors: true
    data_rate: 40MHz
    
    # Optional rendering lambda block
    lambda: |-
      it.fill(Color::BLACK);
      it.print(it.get_width() / 2, it.get_height() / 2, id(font_default), Color::WHITE, TextAlign::CENTER, "M5Stick S3");

# Minimal font component required to display text in the lambda
font:
  - file: "gcode://Roboto-Regular.ttf" # or your chosen TrueType font file local/URL path
    id: font_default
    size: 16

