AI Overview       
To configure the ST7789P3 display on your M5StickS3 using ESPHome,
use the following block configuration. Modern versions of ESPHome 
recommend the mipi_spi platform for ST7789 drivers.

Pin Mapping Reference
The exact hardware pinouts required to map the display signals to the 
onboard ESP32-S3 are:
SPI Clock (SCK): GPIO40
SPI Data (MOSI): GPIO39
Chip Select (CS): GPIO41
Data/Command (DC/RS): GPIO45
Reset (RST): GPIO21
Backlight: GPIO3


spi:
  clk_pin: GPIO40
  mosi_pin: GPIO39

display:
  - platform: mipi_spi
    model: ST7789V
    id: m5stick_display
    width: 135
    height: 240
    offset_width: 52   # Adjust if your image shifts or shows a static edge
    offset_height: 40  # Adjust if your image shifts or shows a static edge
    cs_pin: GPIO41
    dc_pin: GPIO45
    reset_pin: GPIO21
    backlight_pin: GPIO38
    rotation: 90
    lambda: |-
      it.fill(Color::BLACK);
      it.print(10, 10, id(font_default), Color::WHITE, "M5StickS3 Ready");


